 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Cloudy days are the best for sunburns, because the UV gets scattered. It' usually the clear days where you' most vulnerable. Your skin, and in particular your face, neck, and tops of your arms. If it feels hot to touch, it's over the limit. Four to five on a scale of one to ten, where zero is nothing. If you're at six or higher, you've been sunburned. As soon as you notice the red, yes, exactly. It protects the skin from building up too much in one go.",
